Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:28:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] feat(frontend): wire the bookings pages and add reference
 lookup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

YG-8, plus the one contract endpoint nothing was calling.

Statuses are the backend's exact enum names. The mock data's 'Completed' never
existed, and its title-case values would never have matched. bookingReference
is what the user sees; the numeric id is what we call the API with (plan 2.5).

A PENDING booking whose hold is still live shows its remaining time and a
Confirm now shortcut, so a half-finished booking is recoverable from the list
rather than quietly expiring.

BookingLookupPage covers GET /api/bookings/reference/{ref}, which was in the
contract but had no UI. The endpoint is user-scoped server-side, so a stranger's
code 404s rather than leaking anything.

Deviation worth flagging: YG-8 says to wait for SZ-1 before building these
cards. SZ-1 has not landed, and waiting would leave nothing to demo, so these
use the enrich.js lookup instead. When SZ-1 ships, delete enrich.js and its
call sites — the pages read the same field names either way.
